<%- include('partials/head') %>

<div class="page-head">
  <h1>RaidProtector Terms of Service</h1>
  <div class="meta">The rules for using RaidProtector</div>
</div>

<div class="prose">
  <p class="updated">Last updated <%= updated %>. Operated by <%= operator %>.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>RaidProtector is in closed beta.</strong> It is offered to servers with a Protection
      Suite licence, it is incomplete, and it will change. During the beta it is configured to
      report what it would have done rather than to act, and you have to turn acting on yourself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    RaidProtector is a Discord bot that detects raids and coordinated abuse, and can respond to
    them. It is operated by the same person as BotApprove and shares that project's dashboard and
    licence. By adding it to a server, signing in to the dashboard, or using a Protection Suite
    licence, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, remove the bot.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can use it</h2>
  <p>
    You must meet Discord's own minimum age requirement for your country and follow the
    <a href="https://discord.com/terms" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Discord Terms of
    Service</a>. To add RaidProtector to a server you must have the Manage Server permission there,
    which means you are authorised to make that decision for that community.
  </p>
  <p>
    RaidProtector is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated
    by Discord.
  </p>

  <h2>What it does, and what it does not promise</h2>
  <p>
    RaidProtector watches for the patterns that accompany a raid: bursts of joins from young
    accounts, the same message repeated across many channels, many accounts posting in unison. It
    is a safety tool, not a guarantee. It is provided <strong>as is</strong>, without warranty of
    any kind. In particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Detection is based on heuristics and thresholds. It will produce false positives and it
      will miss real attacks.</li>
    <li>It cannot act on anyone whose top role sits at or above its own, and it cannot act on the
      server owner at all.</li>
    <li>It depends on Discord's API and gateway, which can be slow, rate limited, or
      unavailable.</li>
    <li>A sufficiently patient attacker who stays under your thresholds will not trigger it.</li>
    <li>It is not a substitute for Discord's own verification levels, AutoMod, or having awake
      moderators.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You remain responsible for your server's security and for its moderation decisions. Do not
    treat RaidProtector as your only safeguard.
  </p>

  <h2>You are responsible for what it does in your server</h2>
  <p>
    RaidProtector can be configured to time out, kick or ban members. Those settings are yours.
    When it acts, it acts as a moderator of your server, on thresholds you chose, and the
    consequences for the people affected are your responsibility as the server's operator.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every automated action is written to your audit trail with the reason and the signal that
      triggered it.</li>
    <li>A circuit breaker stands the feature down after several separate incidents in a short
      window, so a misconfiguration cannot run away with your member list. It counts incidents
      rather than actions, because timing out a hundred accounts during one real raid is the
      correct outcome.</li>
    <li>Anything taken away can be given back, and the notification tells you how.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you are unsure, leave it in report-only mode. That is the default and it is a legitimate
    way to run the bot permanently.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the automated actions to target individuals for reasons unrelated to genuine raid or
      abuse activity, including personal disputes, or membership of a protected group.</li>
    <li>Configure thresholds designed to catch a specific person rather than a pattern of abuse.</li>
    <li>Use the bot to collect information about members for any purpose other than moderating
      your own server.</li>
    <li>Resell, sublicense or rebrand the service.</li>
    <li>Attempt to overwhelm, reverse engineer for attack purposes, or interfere with the service
      or the infrastructure it runs on.</li>
    <li>Deliberately trigger the bot in someone else's server to get members punished.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Access can be withdrawn from a server or a person for any of the above, without a refund where
    the breach is deliberate.
  </p>

  <h2>Licensing and payment</h2>
  <p>
    RaidProtector's paid features are covered by <strong>Protection Suite</strong>, the same
    licence that covers BotApprove's premium features. One purchase covers both bots for the
    server it was bought for. There is no separate RaidProtector subscription and no separate
    charge.
  </p>
  <p>
    Paid features are switched off until you turn them on, even when the licence is active,
    because several of them change how your server behaves.
  </p>
  <p>
    Payment, renewal, refunds and cancellation are handled under the
    <a href="/terms">BotApprove Terms of Service</a>, which govern the licence itself. If the two
    documents disagree about billing, that one wins.
  </p>

  <h2>Beta</h2>
  <p>
    During the beta, features may be added, changed or removed without notice, data may be reset,
    and the bot may be unavailable for periods at a time. Default behaviour may change when the
    beta ends; any change that would cause the bot to act where it previously only reported will
    be announced before it takes effect, and will not be applied to your server without you
    switching it on.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability</h2>
  <p>
    There is no uptime guarantee. The service may be interrupted for maintenance, by a Discord
    outage, or because something broke. Where a paid licence is affected by a prolonged outage,
    get in touch.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for indirect or
    consequential loss, for damage resulting from a raid the bot failed to stop, or for damage
    resulting from an automated action the bot took under settings you chose. Total liability for
    any claim is limited to what you paid in the twelve months before it arose. Nothing here
    excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop at any time by removing the bot from your server. The operator may suspend or
    withdraw access for a breach of these terms, or discontinue the service. If the service is
    discontinued while you hold a paid licence, you will be told, and the licence will be dealt
    with fairly.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may change. Material changes will be noted by the date at the top of this page,
    and announced in the dashboard.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions go through
    <a href="<%= contactUrl %>" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="updated">
    See also the <a href="/raidprotector/privacy">RaidProtector Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
